		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: radio does not retain RADIO ID/TGs nor contacts not retained in channels on CPS]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5054&amp;p=36731#p36731"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>3 problems with most recent BETA cps and/or DM-1701 radio   <br>1.  CPS doesn't write DMR ID to radio i.e. channel details show "DMR ID:None"<br>2. in writing channels on CPS either TG list or Contact are accepted but not both <br>3.  Radio is able to make contacts through a local repeater but not through duplex Pi Star MMDVM hotspot.<br><br>I had the <br>DM-7101 working just fine when I had it had set up for my simplex hotspot which seems to have died.<br><br>any ideas/instructions/tips would be greatly appreciated.</div></blockquote>DMR ID:None is the normal state as all channels use the DMR ID from the general CPS setting "DMR ID and callsign" unless it's override<br>by a channel specific DMR ID.<br>You can check and modify the default DMR ID by pressing three time on "#" and then SK2+"#"<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2867">SA0BUX</a> — Sun Apr 13, 2025 7:31 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
	</entry>
