		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: radio does not retain RADIO ID/TGs nor contacts not retained in channels on CPS]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5054&amp;p=36730#p36730"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div><br>2. in writing channels on CPS either TG list or Contact are accepted but not both <br></div></blockquote>These are mutually exclusive.  Either you want it on a single TG or you want the channel to have access to the entire list<br><br><blockquote class="uncited"><div><br>3. Radio is able to make contacts through a local repeater but not through duplex Pi Star MMDVM hotspot.<br></div></blockquote>You didn't calibrate your hotspot frequency, and or your radio frequency.<br><br>To use a hotspot the radio's Tx freq must be within a few hundred Hz or the Hotspot Rx freq.<br><br>Real repeaters are less fussy about the freq of the received signal.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Sun Apr 13, 2025 7:21 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
